WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.370
An old legend: a reward paid
in rice, on a chessboard.

2
00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:07.610
One grain on the first square.

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.140
Two on the second.

4
00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:10.930
Four on the third.

5
00:00:10.980 --> 00:00:13.570
Each square doubles the one before.

6
00:00:13.620 --> 00:00:18.850
By the end of the first row, square eight
holds one hundred and twenty-eight grains.

7
00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:20.960
There are sixty-four squares.

8
00:00:21.010 --> 00:00:23.450
How much rice is on the whole board?

9
00:00:23.500 --> 00:00:24.410
A sackful?

10
00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:25.800
Far more?

11
00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:28.920
In this mission, you'll
meet geometric sequences,

12
00:00:28.970 --> 00:00:33.850
where each term is the one before
multiplied by a common ratio, r.

13
00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:39.640
You'll find any term with u n equals u
one times r to the power n minus one.

14
00:00:39.690 --> 00:00:42.180
And you'll add the terms with one formula,

15
00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.050
instead of one by one.

16
00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.850
Your mission: work out how much
rice is on all sixty-four squares.
